body:
I encountered this. Init with your offset values. Then as soon as you set loading to true, set your variable that is your offset to 0, then after loading, set the value of that variable back to your offset value. It did the trick for me after hours of delving into it. I included some other parameters to get a clean solution with Android and iOS.

Initialize variables : 

```
this.scrollOffsetValue = getHeaderHeight() + 55;
this.scrollOffset = this.scrollOffsetValue;
```

Params for Flatlist :

```
contentInset={{ top: this.scrollOffset }}
contentOffset={{ y: -this.scrollOffset, }}

//

refreshControl={
   <RefreshControl
       refreshing={this.state.gettingFeed}
       onRefresh={() => this.refreshFeed()}
       progressViewOffset={160}
     />
}
ListHeaderComponent = {<View style={{width:'100%',height: Platform.os=="android" ? this.scrollOffsetValue : 0 }} />}

```

on load start :

`this.scrollOffset=0;`

on load done and time to render : 

`this.scrollOffset = this.scrollOffsetValue;`

Good luck, this works on Android and iOS for differing header sizes.
